  {
    "id": "q01",
    "view": {
      "mode": "single",
      "stem": "Find the arithmetic square roots of $4.3,6.2,8.9,10,50,75$ using the supplied table. Supplementary reporting condition for this question: retain the full table approximations and also report each to the nearest $0.1$, not by truncation. This added display condition is not a historical table rule. Which complete record is correct, in the listed radicand order?\n\nTable IV (Square roots), literal excerpt from V. M. Bradis, *Four-figure Mathematical Tables*, Drofa, Moscow, 2010, 13th stereotype edition, printed pages 35, 36, 37, 38. Decimal commas are shown as decimal points.\nFor a row below 10, main column $c$ refers to $N+0.01c$; for a row at least 10, it refers to $N+0.1c$. A correction column refers to the fourth significant argument digit, and its integer is in units of $0.001$ of the root.\n\n| Row N | Main column : entry | Correction column : integer | Next main column : entry |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 4.3 | 0 : 2.074 | - | - |\n| 6.2 | 0 : 2.490 | - | - |\n| 8.9 | 0 : 2.983 | - | - |\n| 10 | 0 : 3.162 | - | - |\n| 50 | 0 : 7.071 | - | - |\n| 75 | 0 : 8.660 | - | - |",
      "figure_ids": [],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Root approximations: $(-2.074,-2.490,-2.983,-3.162,-7.071,-8.660)$; reports to $0.1$: $(-2.1,-2.5,-3.0,-3.2,-7.1,-8.7)$.",
          "figure_ids": []
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Root approximations: $(2.074,2.490,2.983,3.162,7.071,8.660)$; reports to $0.1$: $(2.0,2.4,2.9,3.1,7.0,8.6)$.",
          "figure_ids": []
